<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from intervening in the banking system Monday, traders said.</p>
<p>Economists had forecast no Fed open market operations despite a slight add need.  A 14-day system repurchase agreement remains outstanding.</p>
<p>At the Fed's normal intervention time of 1030 EDT/1430 GMT, fed funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent, near the Fed's current official target level of 5.50 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
